# layer-contract-conformance-b is a shard driver: it execs the sibling layer-contract-conformance/run.sh --group b, so it shares the parent's declaration shape.
# The validator walks the whole distribution tree and renders its arm map via render-invariant-index.sh; VERSION is the renderer's root marker.
!scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh
scripts/
# reason: core/ is walked by content -- the validator the parent run.sh runs (layer-contract-conformance/run.sh:750) finds every core/*.sh and derives core/*/, scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh:2476 and :3327.
core/
templates/
.githooks/
patterns/
.claude/rules/
docs/
CLAUDE.md
VERSION
